// What a learner's log says about one concept, as five counts: attempts, misses
// (wrong, or tapped out), clean answers (right, no hints, no tap-out), sure
// errors (a miss made at confidence 90 or more) and whether the latest attempt
// was fluent (clean, confident and quick). Only attempts at items linked to the
// concept count, and an attempt still pending a verdict counts as nothing. The
// presentation policy and the choice of the next kind of exercise both read it,
// so both see the same history. plan_tally_until reads the first `upto` events,
// which is how "the history before this attempt" is asked.

plan_item_in_concept(Plan_book plan_book, int plan_item_number, int plan_concept_number) {
  int plan_at = 0;
  int plan_linked = 0;
  while (plan_at < len(plan_book.links.link_items)) {
    plan_linked = plan_linked || (plan_book.links.link_items[plan_at] == plan_item_number && plan_book.links.link_concepts[plan_at] == plan_concept_number);
    plan_at = plan_at + 1;
  }
} return int plan_linked;
(Plan_book(Plan_catalog(["c", "d"], ["i", "j"], [1000, 1000]), Plan_links([0, 1, 1], [0, 0, 1], [0, 0, 0]), Plan_needs([], [])), 1, 1):(1)
